  "question": "# Complete field payment for the retained complement-relaxed He-3 trial\n\nCalculate or rigorously bound the complete paid energy of the frozen product family phi_tau tensor chi_i against its stated fragment lower. Keep all pre-existing mass/lane controls and leave tau as a conditional variable.\n\nIn particular recover separately the normalized complete field expectation F_full=<Hf(A_internal+A_cross)> and quadratic crossing self-counterterm C_cross=epsilon^2<int A_cross^dagger A_cross/omega> on the SAME original complete chi_i, or derive a direct complete relaxed-field bound. Retain the actual full Gram, positive source promotion, both physical helicities, original infinite-frequency profile, all self/mixed counterterms, massive photon/matter recoil, normal EDGE/gate, preparation and signed common-reference terms.\n\nUse sources/TRIAL_FAMILY.json and the hashed owning source records. Its finite placement ground family is supplied as background definition; the question is the complete payment on the retained field/matter trial. Use actual source matrices and applicable installed native capabilities with source-bound receipts. Keep native execution, analytical inequalities and engine-free replay distinct. Existing aggregate paid uppers cannot be split into components without deriving their signed decomposition.\n\nDetermine what conditional tau intervals, if any, the resulting COMPLETE upper certifies below the fragment lower. Report unsuccessful controls and exactly which needed operand or hypothesis remains if certification cannot be obtained. An upper that does not certify is not a lower bound on the actual energy. Make no nuclear mass/radius assignment or binding fit. The intrinsic recipient and the positive crossing-gate recipient retain their actual identity-baseline difference.\n\nNo expected sign or parameter interval is supplied. No new trial optimization, field cutoff, changed coefficient, source truncation or second research window is authorized by this case. If a new construction is needed, identify it precisely as follow-up.\n",
